// A HELD RESUME THROUGH A `!Alloc` CALLEE — the spine callee's row is blind.
// `plus_one` declares `!Alloc` and calls its callback; the callback resumes a
// held continuation, so `plus_one`'s own remainder (`+ 1`) is captured into
// the continuation record when the resume runs — inside `plus_one`'s frame,
// under its own `!Alloc`. The op's row is priced (`bump` is held, so it
// carries `Memory + Alloc` at its perform), but nothing carries that cost
// into the declaration whose remainder is what gets captured: the callback
// performs no op, so the gate on `f` sees a Pure row and admits it. The
// program compiles, runs to 21, and `plus_one`'s absence proof is false.
// DECLARED RED (frontier_expected_red) until the continuation's cost reaches
// every frame the spine extends
// (Hβ.continuations.spine-callee-row-is-blind-to-the-held-resume).
effect Cell {
  bump() -> Int
}

fn plus_one(f) with !Alloc = f() + 1

handler cell with s = 10 {
  bump() => plus_one(() => resume(s)),
}

fn body() = bump() * 2

fn main() = {
  body()
} ~> cell
